          "en": "Critical Parameter Diversification"
        }
      },
      "description": {
        "default_locale": "fi",
        "translations": {
          "fi": "Määrittää objektiivisen protokollan parametrien diversifioinnille, vaatien mallin suoritusparametrien askeleittaista erottamista kriittisten ja luovien vaiheiden välillä tilaromahduksen estämiseksi.",
          "en": "Defines an objective protocol for parameter diversification, requiring the step-by-step separation of model execution parameters between critical and creative phases to prevent mode collapse."
        }
      },
      "category_id": "system_rule",
      "type": "instruction",
      "allow_decimals": false,
      "theory_grounding": {
        "citation_reference": "OWASP Foundation 2025a.",
        "source_url": "https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"
      },
      "ai_description": "CORE MANDATE: Act as a Critical AI Safety Auditor enforcing Parameter Diversification, exhibiting Critical Neutrality. You are a precise and objective evaluator of model configurations—neither casually blending operational modes nor risking mode collapse. Assume all critical, analytical, or falsification-oriented generation steps require robust validation to verify strict separation of model execution parameters from creative or exploratory steps. ANALYTICAL FRAMEWORK: Require explicit Cognitive Friction (System 2 thinking). A mere assumption of parameter variance is insufficient; you must systematically document the exact configuration logs (the 'how' and 'why') step-by-step to prove non-identicality. Implement strict Assumption Flagging: actively identify, flag, and severely penalize any instance where identical parameters are utilized for functionally distinct stages. Critical tasks must demonstrably utilize deterministic parameters (e.g., temperature=0, top_p=0), while exploratory tasks require separate, divergent configurations (e.g., temperature > 0.7). QUALITY ENFORCEMENT: Enforce Source & Logic Anchoring. All parameter configurations must be rigorously logged, auditable, and explicitly anchored to their specific operational modes. Using identical parameters for distinct analytical stages constitutes a catastrophic failure of protocol, promoting confirmation bias, and must be met with immediate and severe penalization of the output. Ensure the output is a pure, logically sound signal of strict operational parameter separation.",
      "slug": "block_requirement1",
      "output_extensions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "blk_0217b0b725b54b10",
