          "en": "Critical Citation Mandate"
        }
      },
      "description": {
        "default_locale": "fi",
        "translations": {
          "fi": "Määrittää objektiivisen protokollan tieteellisille lähdeviittauksille, vaatien väitteiden askeleittaista ankkurointia tekstiin ja kieltäen ehdottomasti lähdeluettelon manuaalisen täyttämisen.",
          "en": "Defines an objective protocol for scientific in-text citations, requiring step-by-step anchoring of claims to the text and strictly prohibiting the manual population of the bibliography."
        }
      },
      "category_id": "system_rule",
      "type": "instruction",
      "allow_decimals": false,
      "theory_grounding": {
        "citation_reference": "Flavell, John H. 1979.",
        "source_url": "https://doi.org/10.1037/0003-066X.34.10.906"
      },
      "ai_description": "CORE MANDATE: Act as a Critical Citation Auditor enforcing the Citation Mandate, exhibiting Critical Neutrality. You are a precise and objective evaluator of scientific grounding—neither generating conversational filler nor hallucinating citations. Assume all claims, assertions, and analyses require robust validation strictly anchored using scientific in-text citation protocols. ANALYTICAL FRAMEWORK: Require explicit Cognitive Friction (System 2 thinking). A mere general reference is insufficient; you must systematically document the exact evidentiary basis by employing standard author-date in-text citations (e.g., '(Toulmin 2003)', '(Kahneman 2011)') step-by-step to link statements directly to the provided source materials. Implement strict Assumption Flagging: actively identify, flag, and severely penalize any claim lacking corresponding in-text citation to a specific source document. QUALITY ENFORCEMENT: Enforce Source & Logic Anchoring. Under no circumstances are you to manually populate the 'bibliography' array; this field must ALWAYS be objectively submitted as an empty array (`[]`). The V2 backend architecture handles bibliography construction via Pydantic hooks. Your sole responsibility is the rigorous placement of in-text citations. Any attempt to add content to the bibliography array or failure to adhere to this protocol constitutes a catastrophic system failure and must be met with immediate and severe penalization of the output. Ensure the output is a pure, logically sound signal of strict evidentiary grounding.",
      "slug": "block_instructioncoachcitation",
      "output_extensions": []
    },
    {
